 "note": "PASS at the standard gate (56/56 at dE 16; IoU min .854, dE mean 13.7, max 15.8). LIVE RIG PASSES since round 26: the cap gores are flat per-face materials (beenie.py gore_faces, the same azimuth split as the shader; the live renderer keeps only Principled values, so the shader gores had rendered as one grey dome: live dE 17.3 -> 14.1 vs Cycles 13.7), and the back view f115 was re-optimised alone (tmp/hold_pose.py: yaw 270.5 -> 275.7, IoU .858 -> .881) because its live silhouette sat .009 under the published one. Round 25: the source draws the propeller as a THICK red band over the cap and a long red bill -- prop_h 0.7 (was .35) and bill_l 4.0 (was 2.4) took dE mean 14.4 -> 13.7 and f99-f101 (16.5-17.2) under 16. The Beenie (beenie.py on the kid rig): a WHITE-FACED CLOWN (kid.py smile: a red U curve on the face surface + a red nose, dark blue eye sockets), a SIX-gore propeller beanie (cap_reps 2: opposite gores alike, R/G/B, cap_turn 120 -- the source shows the same gores facing left and right), the green blaster in the RIGHT hand (gun_hand f: the rig's far arm; front views show its muzzle at the viewer's left). Views (per-frame yaw priors): right cycle f66-f73, turn f74-f79, FRONT cycle f80-f90 (it was fitted side-on under an old yaw-0 prior), turn f91-f95, left cycle f96-f105, turn f106-f113, back cycle f114-f121. Round 16: 1 -> 53/56 at dE 16.",
